## Error recovery map
codex command not found -> command -v codex; inspect PATH; do not edit repo yet.
unknown Codex flag -> run codex --help or codex SUBCOMMAND --help, then retry with the local syntax.
config unknown field -> run codex --strict-config --help; inspect relevant config key; remove or rename only the bad key after backup.
TOML duplicate key -> inspect exact duplicate with rg; back up; remove only stale duplicate.
hooks not running -> inspect [features] hooks, hook source, matcher, hook trust/state, project trust, and whether project .codex layers load.
hook command not found -> inspect absolute path, executable availability, script permissions, cwd, and managed_dir rules.
skill not found -> inspect discovery path, SKILL.md frontmatter, [skills.config], bundled skills, and current working directory.
AGENTS ignored -> inspect cwd, repo root, AGENTS.override.md, fallback filenames, max bytes, and project trust.
warm imp stale -> rely on source fingerprint hot reload; if still stale, run imps stop imp-codex if available, then retry.

## Mutation policy
Codex repository edits are allowed only when the user explicitly asks to change local Codex/imps behavior and the target file has been inspected.

Before editing, check git status and read the narrow target files. Patch the smallest relevant file set and verify with focused tests or help commands.

Do not modify auth files, secrets, unrelated repo files, package metadata, or generated artifacts unless explicitly requested and necessary for the task. Only confirm auth file presence, paths, and permissions.

Do not commit, push, install packages, change global config, or run destructive git commands unless the user explicitly asks for that action.

